```
==================================================================
Detection Name : LotL - VSSAdmin Shadow Copy Deletion / Certutil Abuse
MITRE ATT&CK   : T1490 (Inhibit System Recovery) - vssadmin
                 T1218 (System Binary Proxy Execution) - certutil
Log Source     : Sysmon Operational (Event ID 1 - Process Create)
Purpose        : Detect native Windows binaries being abused to
                 delete shadow copies (common pre-ransomware step)
                 or to download/decode payloads via certutil.
==================================================================
*/

index=lotl_lab
    ("vssadmin.exe" "delete shadows")
    OR
    ("certutil.exe" ("-urlcache" OR "-decode" OR "-decodehex"))
| rex field=_raw "Image:\s*(?<Image>[^\r\n]+)"
| rex field=_raw "CommandLine:\s*(?<CommandLine>[^\r\n]+)"
| rex field=_raw "ParentImage:\s*(?<ParentImage>[^\r\n]+)"
| table _time, host, Image, CommandLine, ParentImage
| sort -_time
```

--------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTES
--------------------------------------------------------------------
- This query was validated against real Sysmon Event ID 1 telemetry
  generated by running:
      vssadmin.exe delete shadows /for=C: /quiet
  on a Windows Server 2022 EC2 instance running Sysmon v15.22.

- The rex extractions exist because the lab evidence was ingested
  into Splunk via a flat CSV export (Get-WinEvent | Export-Csv).
  In a production deployment where logs are shipped through the
  Splunk Universal Forwarder + Windows TA for Sysmon, the fields
  Image, CommandLine, and ParentImage are auto-extracted by Splunk,
  so the three `rex` lines can be removed and the query simplifies to:

      index=lotl_lab sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
          EventCode=1
          (Image="*\\vssadmin.exe" CommandLine="*delete*shadows*")
          OR
          (Image="*\\certutil.exe" (CommandLine="*-urlcache*" OR CommandLine="*-decode*"))
      | table _time, host, Image, CommandLine, ParentImage
      | sort -_time

- To turn this into a live alert (requires Splunk Enterprise, not Free):
    1. Save As -> Alert
    2. Trigger condition: Number of Results > 0
    3. Schedule: run every 15 minutes over "Last 24 hours"
    4. Action: add to Notable Events / send email / webhook to SOAR
